# core.autocrlf=true is on for this checkout, and it would rewrite
# evidence/weapon-material/artifacts.sha256 with CRLF on checkout. Every line of
# that file is `sha256 *<path>`, so a trailing CR becomes part of the filename and
# `sha256sum -c` reports all 28 lines as "No such file" -- the receipt would be
# uncheckable in exactly the situation it exists for (a fresh clone).
evidence/weapon-material/artifacts.sha256 -text
